WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.037
Week 24: Commands, Advice, and Procedures. give a safe procedure offer advice distinguish request from order

2
00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:20.876
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can give a safe procedure, offer advice, distinguish request from order. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:20.876 --> 00:00:29.553
Language system. Tú, usted, ustedes, and nosotros commands; pronoun placement; negative commands; deber and conviene.

4
00:00:29.553 --> 00:00:36.736
Sound and delivery. Command prominence softened by por favor, intonation, and conditional phrasing.

5
00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:46.269
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:46.269 --> 00:01:12.335
Model language. Apague el equipo antes de abrirlo. — Turn off the equipment before opening it. No compartas esa contraseña. — Do not share that password. Asegúrense de guardar una copia. — Make sure you save a copy. Comprobemos los datos otra vez. — Let's check the data again. Conviene evitar este camino de noche. — It is advisable to avoid this road at night.

7
00:01:12.335 --> 00:01:22.339
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
